  "sourceFixtureSha256": "1797662bbf32b6e5cad08e3acd758346599f0defbfe344a4f43380420890c231",
  "adoption": {
    "eligibility": "Original NEI_GT_API_Config only registers maps with mNEIAllowed. Restore all 85 native machine/eight fuel flags; hidden compatibility/auxiliary pools remain registered and retain recipes and lookup. No standalone Assembler invented.",
    "captions": "Original NEI_RecipeMap.drawExtras controls unspecified tier/tier/power via mShowVoltageAmperageInNEI, and omits usage for absolute unit power when voltage is hidden. Total cost/gain still shown; existing native time and crucible/Fusion specialization retained.",
    "bridging": "Modern adapter: when EMI is loaded, its native machine rows are the sole machine browser provider. JEI machine categories remain registered but no machine rows are sent to its EMI bridge; separate manual tool assembly remains registered. This extends the existing loot/structure/geology bridge suppression.",
    "viewport": "Modern EMI can clamp the requested recipe height. Fit original 176x146 content uniformly to the actual public WidgetHolder viewport, preserving native SlotWidget identity, hitboxes, tooltips and recipe context. The recipe schema and relative slot coordinates are retained. EMI API behavior inspected in the preserved official work/emi-sources.jar; no EMI implementation source copied.",
